  "finalText": "I built the sequence as a 10 s, 1920×1080, 30 fps composition on a #0B0B0F background with #FF5A1F orange. It is timed to 120 BPM, so one beat is 0.5 s. I checked it on a contact sheet at eight frames; I didn't run the critic or play it back in real time.\n\n- **Flashes (0.5–3.5 s):** each feature word cuts in on its own bar and is hidden again by the next orange wipe.\n  - **40h battery** (0.5 s): the wipe crosses left to right and the word punches in from 135% scale.\n  - **Spatial audio** (1.5 s): the wipe runs right to left and the word drops in from above.\n  - **Pure silence** (2.5 s): the wipe rises from the bottom and the word scales up from 60%.\n  - Each word has a small orange 01/02/03 tag above it. The half-second after the last word is left empty before the slam.\n- **PULSE 2 (4.0 s):** it slams in from 320% scale with a short camera-style shake and an orange flash. An orange ring and a thinner white ring expand and fade, and an orange underline wipes in from its left edge.\n- **Available now (7.0 s):** PULSE 2 moves up and shrinks, then an orange pill springs in with \"Available now\" in dark text. That lockup holds until 10 s.\n\nMarkers sit at 0.5, 1.5, 2.5, 4.0 and 6.5 s. I used Expo easing throughout.\n\nOffers for next tweaks:\n- Add a subtle beat-pulse on the pill.\n- Cut each flash to a single beat (0.5 s) for a more frantic feel.\n- Add sound effects.\nI stretched each word's hold so it's readable for about 0.97 s, and the critic score went from 55 to 78. I left the remaining notes alone: the fast wipes and 1 s word spacing are deliberate for the 120 BPM cut."
